edit('sections/01-introduction.tex',r'\textbf{Directional calibration transfer.} The GLM cancellation/return point contrast is $+20.8/-17.3$ BA points, with paired 95\% intervals $[-12.6,35.3]/[-38.2,-5.3]$. Thus the return reduction is resolved, while the cancellation direction remains uncertain.',r'\textbf{Calibration stability and deployment cost.} The GLM cancellation/return point contrast is $+20.8/-17.3$ BA points. We test all eight contrasts with customer-paired permutations and Holm correction, and rebuild calibration over 100 training-customer resamples to separate source changes from sampling and attacker-fit sensitivity.')
